    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">1. Overview</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This is the <strong>3D printing master plan</strong>.
            The site-wide
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN') %]" class="doc-link">MASTER_PLAN</a>
            only indexes it. Child plans stay the spec for their own work.
            This page is the overall view: what <code>printing_3d</code> is,
            which plans exist, and in what order they should move.</p>
            <div class="doc-info">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Not this document:</strong>
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/3d_printing') %]" class="doc-link">3d_printing</a>
                is the operator knowledge base (how to use the live module).
                App URLs such as <code>/3d</code> belong there, not on MASTER_PLAN.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-success">
                <p class="doc-body">Open the attached project and this plan standalone:</p>
                <div class="doc-navrow">
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=206" class="doc-navlink" title="Project #206 3DPRINT — parent of INV, File Mgmt, Sales, DRYER-INT.">Project #206 3DPRINT</a>
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo') %]?project_id=206" class="doc-navlink" title="Todos attached to #206.">Todos on #206</a>
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN') %]" class="doc-navlink" title="Site-wide coordinator. This 3D plan is one entry there.">MASTER_PLAN</a>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="what" class="doc-h2">2. What the 3D printing system is</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">A <strong>production provider</strong> for a site that
            has the <code>printing_3d</code> module on. Inventory/Accounting is the
            commerce and stock source of truth. 3D owns printers, STL/3MF models,
            the print queue, and filament reserve/issue refs
            <code>3D-JOB-{id}</code> / <code>3D-SALE-{id}</code>.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Farm</strong> — printers, queue, staff-prep before print, complete with grams so stock is issued.</li>
                <li><strong>Library</strong> — models linked to inventory items; geometry for grams (STL; 3MF must be extracted).</li>
                <li><strong>Project import</strong> — a downloaded pack becomes assemblies + BOM + hardware + print jobs, not one row per zip/3MF plate.</li>
                <li><strong>Signs</strong> — herb/sign STL via the OpenSCAD service; same model/job tables.</li>
                <li><strong>Storefront</strong> — browse/shop consume inventory; <code>/3d/store</code> redirects to Shop/Cart (Inventory-owned).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Tree:
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=38" class="doc-link">#38 3dPrinting</a>
            →
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=206" class="doc-link">#206 3DPRINT</a>
            → #207 INV, #208 File Mgmt, #209 Sales,
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=272" class="doc-link">#272 DRYER-INT</a>.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="plans" class="doc-h2">3. Child plans (this coordinator links them)</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Plan</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Project</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Role</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/DryerProjectImportPlan') %]" class="doc-link">DryerProjectImportPlan</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=272" class="doc-link">#272 DRYER-INT</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Test scenario: PDF is the BOM; 3MF files are plates of labeled parts; base unit vs add-on module; hardware lines.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/SignGenerator') %]" class="doc-link">SignGenerator</a>
                    (MASTER_PLAN also cites HerbSignGeneratorPlan — that filename is not on this tree)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">#206 / signs</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Herb/sign STL via OpenSCAD service; same <code>printing_3d_models</code>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">3dBrowseGalleryPlan
                    (cited on MASTER_PLAN; file not on this tree)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">#206</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Public browse vs farm console; STL thumbnails. Restore or rewrite before treating as live spec.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/3d_printing') %]" class="doc-link">3d_printing</a> (operator KB, not a plan)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">#206</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">How to use the running module. Not a substitute for this coordinator.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="order" class="doc-h2">4. Work order</h2>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Domain model</strong> — assemblies, BOM qty, hardware vs printed, filament type. Dryer PDF is the current proof that plate-level import is not a BOM.</li>
                <li><strong>Import playbook</strong> — DryerProjectImportPlan v0.22+: scan manual → part SKUs → extract STL → items + BOM → order a config → explode to jobs.</li>
                <li><strong>Farm</strong> — queue any item, change filament, grams from STL or manual, issue on complete.</li>
                <li><strong>Signs / browse</strong> — after import+queue are honest; do not rebuild tables.</li>
                <li><strong>Commerce</strong> — shop/cart/order stay on Inventory; 3d is the production provider.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="cross" class="doc-h2">5. Cross-plan (raise, do not absorb)</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
